  "id": "COMPOUND:18068 - PROTEIN:367",
  "verbalization": "Chinikomycin B is shown to have a target relationship with Serine--tRNA ligase, cytoplasmic, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including [(8R,9S,10R,13R,14R,17S)-17-[(1R)-1-[(2R)-4,5-dimethyl-6-oxo-2,3-dihydropyran-2-yl]-1-hydroxyethyl]-14-hydroxy-10-methyl-1-oxo-7,8,9,11,12,15,16,17-octahydro-4H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-13-yl]methyl acetate and rel-(6R,7R)-1,5,6,7-Tetrahydro-6,7-dihydroxy-7-methyl-3-(1E,3E)-1,3-pentadien-1-yl-8H-2-benzopyran-8-one. All these compounds are implicated in the regulation of S-methylmethionine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase BHMT2, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the targeting of Serine--tRNA ligase, cytoplasmic. The evidence suggests that Chinikomycin B may act through a similar pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of Serine--tRNA ligase, cytoplasmic, which is a key enzyme in the methylation cycle. This integrated evidence highlights the potential for Chinikomycin B to interact with BHMT2 via a shared regulatory mechanism, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
